{"id":"000W17","title":"Combined Sandwiches","author":"RockyRoer","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":3,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-13T09:39:35+00:00","posted":"Heute, 09:44 Uhr","rules":"The Rules:\n\n• [Sudoku]: Normal sudoku rules apply - fill every row, column, and 3x3 box with the digits from 1 to 9 once each.\n\n• [Combined Sandwiches]: Every cell in the grid has a possible 'clue value' equal to the sum of the sandwich clues for its row and its column. A sandwich clue is the sum of the digits between the cells containing 1 and 9 in that row or column.\n\nA clue outside the grid is giving the 'clue value' of the cell in the X-Th cell in that row or column from the direction of the clue where x is the digit in the cell next to the clue.\n\n• E.g. if R1C1 is 5, then Row 5 and Column 1 must have sandwich sums that sum to 30 -- e.g. 20 and 10, or 0 and 30.\n\nThe Puzzle:\n\nTry it using Sven's Sudokupad","solutionCode":"Row 2","tags":["Sudoku","Sandwich (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/22lhzcbclm","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/22lhzcbclm","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":11,"cols":11,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-13T09:39:35+00:00"}